  "slug": "laser-dynamics-32ea",
  "summary": "Theoretical cavity proposals treat nonlinearity, asymmetric dissipation, Floquet driving, and PT symmetry as explicit control parameters.",
  "synthesis": "The three preprints share a common thread: engineering coherent control in driven, coupled cavity systems by tailoring nonlinear terms, dissipation, or sideband driving. The first derives analytic optimal conditions for unconventional photon blockade in coupled cavities with second-order nonlinearity and asymmetric dissipation, targeting robust antibunching. The second proposes a Floquet sideband method to manipulate mechanical dark modes in a three-mode optomechanical system, supported by fidelity and population analyses. The third applies PT-symmetric cavity optomechanics, using second-order sidebands and tunable slow-fast light, to magnetometry with theoretical picotesla-level sensitivity. What is new in each case is the explicit use of nonlinearity, asymmetric dissipation, Floquet driving, or PT symmetry as control parameters. All listed works are theoretical, and their summaries report no experimental validation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
